3
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:22,020
It was kind of a small regional seminar, and it was happening at the church that Drew

4
00:00:22,020 --> 00:00:28,460
is a, I believe he's an elder or a leader at, and I got to be honest, he set up a table

5
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:32,160
because it was his local church, and it was a small regional gathering, and there was

6
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:35,300
like 20 of us getting cookies where he had his table set up, and I've been that guy,

7
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:39,720
so I'm like, you got to go talk to the guy, you know, he came all this way, well, you know,

8
00:00:39,720 --> 00:00:45,520
he set up a table, so I'm like, I'll go listen to his spiel, hear what he has to say, pat

9
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:49,320
him on the back, say thanks for your ministry, brother, and we'll move on, and you know, he'll

10
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:51,220
feel good, and I'll feel good, and it'll be great.

11
00:00:51,220 --> 00:00:57,940
And you guys have all been to tables like that in some way, shape, or form, and Drew

12
00:00:57,940 --> 00:01:04,080
just was so kind, and listened, and shared, and he did not try to sell me anything.

13
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:06,440
He actually tried to undersell me everything.

14
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:09,580
He was just like, I'm just here to, I love the church, and I want to help the church, and

15
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:11,120
if we never talk again, that's great.

16
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:16,800
I hope this conversation helps you help your church, and I was like, he was almost so underselling

17
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:20,300
himself that I like, out of spite, wanted him to sell me more.

18
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:27,840
And so, yeah, that's how I met Drew, and you know, I, as a pastor, someone who grew up in

19
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:31,580
the church, I feel like I had my finances somewhat in order, and I was like, I'm sure he could

20
00:01:31,580 --> 00:01:35,060
help me, but at this point in my life, is it something that I should prioritize?

21
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:38,760
And thank the Lord that we have spouses sometimes.

22
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:41,820
Because my wife said, no, we need to talk to this guy about our money.

23
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:49,080
So we did, and it was incredibly impactful for me, and for Marissa, and for the way that

24
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:50,960
we view everything that God gives us.

25
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:58,580
Drew was so kind, so pastoral, so wise, and it actually came at the perfect time for us.

26
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:02,760
And even then, I was like, oh, I'm so glad that he helped me, again, for free, didn't

27
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:05,620
ask for anything, didn't try and sell me.

28
00:02:05,620 --> 00:02:07,500
Now that I've helped you, you should let me help your church.

29
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:13,700
Didn't do any of that, and I was still a little bit skeptical about bringing this opportunity

30
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:14,380
to you all.

31
00:02:14,380 --> 00:02:19,840
And the Lord has just been trying to work on me, and he's been doing so.

32
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:25,280
And so it just, the timing of this is perfect, and I'm really excited for this seminar.

33
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:29,800
I hope that it blesses many of you, it blesses our congregation, and it trickles down to the

34
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:34,040
way that we can have a kingdom impact in our city, which is something that we talk about

35
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:34,440
a lot.

36
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:36,640
So I'm going to invite Pastor Drew up.

37
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:41,160
I realized that about the middle of the second Song, that I don't think I've ever been put

38
