in a position to say his last name out loud.

39
00:02:43,380 --> 00:02:46,060
Give it your best telemarketing.

40
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:50,560
Pastor Drew Gacy.

41
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:53,060
Gacy, Gacy, Gacy.

42
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:57,120
It's a tough one, but it's great on screening telemarketers.

43
00:02:57,120 --> 00:03:01,960
So very good at screening telemarketers.

44
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:03,480
Well, it is good to be with you.

45
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:05,000
And how many years ago was that?

46
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:05,860
About three years ago?

47
00:03:05,860 --> 00:03:07,180
Am I right in saying that?

48
00:03:07,180 --> 00:03:08,600
I'm telling you.

49
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:10,160
And thank you.

50
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:11,540
That's how I operate.

51
00:03:11,540 --> 00:03:12,720
I'm a pastor.

52
00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:14,920
That's my heart.

53
00:03:14,920 --> 00:03:17,400
It's about his kingdom.

54
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:18,300
Amen, church?

55
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:20,600
Okay.

56
00:03:20,600 --> 00:03:22,800
Got to lay it very clear here.

57
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:24,520
I play the drums.

58
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:26,480
I used to race cars.

59
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:27,740
And I ride a motorcycle.

60
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:28,780
You know what that means?

61
00:03:28,780 --> 00:03:30,880
I can't hear you.

62
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:34,320
So with that in mind, am I on?

63
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:35,740
Oh, is that you?

64
00:03:35,740 --> 00:03:37,400
That's mine.

65
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:38,660
I thought you were going to break something.

66
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:39,840
I'm not going to break anything.

67
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:41,300
That's my little pedal there.

68
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:43,200
So I can't hear you.

69
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:45,320
So I'm going to be looking for some response.

70
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:47,380
But I want to get ourselves going.

71
00:03:47,380 --> 00:03:49,760
We got a full couple days here.

72
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:51,060
And I want to get you.

73
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:52,980
I want to lay the groundwork.

74
00:03:54,720 --> 00:04:01,100
If you walk out of this series that Pastor Ryan has shared these last couple weeks,

75
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:08,620
and you walk out of this and these next couple days falling more in love with money,

76
00:04:08,620 --> 00:04:13,180
instead of falling more in love with the Lord, we have failed you miserably.

77
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:21,920
Our goal is to help you fall more in love with Jesus and allow these tools that God has put into our care,

78
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:28,900
money, finances, resources, things, to be used for his greater purposes and his kingdom.

79
00:04:28,900 --> 00:04:29,640
Amen, church?

80
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:32,600
Now you're getting better, but not there.

81
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:36,540
The caffeinated part did not kick in yet.

82
00:04:36,540 --> 00:04:39,600
But to get ourselves going and moving in the right direction,

83
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:42,200
how many here are familiar with the author Jules Verne?

84
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:43,960
Put your hand up high, real high.

85
00:04:44,500 --> 00:04:46,920
Okay, name me a book that Jules Verne wrote.

86
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:47,280
Somebody.

87
00:04:47,280 --> 00:04:49,960
20,000 Leagues Under the Sea.

88
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:51,860
Usually the first response I get.

89
00:04:51,860 --> 00:04:52,740
Name me another book.

90
00:04:52,740 --> 00:04:55,600
Around the World in 80 Days.

91
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:56,160
What else?

92
00:04:56,160 --> 00:04:57,000
Give me another book.

93
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,580
Journey to the Center of the Earth.

94
00:04:59,580 --> 00:05:00,540
Give me another book.

95
00:05:00,540 --> 00:05:04,260
Have you ever heard of that book, Mysterious Island?

96
00:05:04,260 --> 00:05:07,900
Yeah, people always say yes after I say that.

97
00:05:07,900 --> 00:05:13,840
So let me just give you a little bit of a synopsis of the opening of that book.

98
00:05:14,280 --> 00:05:15,600
I'm going to read it for you.

99
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:20,020
So listen closely because it's going to lay the groundwork for where we want to go.

100
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:26,640
In the book, Mysterious Island by Jules Verne, it opens up with a daring hot air balloon escape of five prisoners.

101
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:31,880
Rather than making it to safety, the wind sent the prisoners out over the ocean.

102
00:05:32,480 --> 00:05:38,480
And that's where things went from bad to worse because they realized that their balloon was losing altitude.

103
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:42,200
They were drifting dangerously close to the waters below.

104
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:48,660
They decided to dump a few of their possessions like spare clothes and weapons in an attempt to regain altitude.

105
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:54,880
And their plan worked at first, but eventually they started to drift lower to the water.

106
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:58,380
Then they decided to throw their food supplies overboard.

107
00:05:58,380 --> 00:06:03,540
They figured it's better to be in the air rather than be drowned in the ocean with a full belly.

108
00:06:03,540 --> 00:06:07,900
Again, the balloon lifted, but only for a short time.

109
00:06:08,420 --> 00:06:14,500
They could see off in the distance some dry land, but it was unlikely that they were going to make it to the shores.

110
00:06:14,500 --> 00:06:22,480
This is when the men decided to do the unthinkable thing and get rid of one of the most essential things that they thought that they had.

111
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:24,940
The basket in which they were standing in.

112
00:06:24,940 --> 00:06:29,800
The men tied themselves to the balloon and they cut the basket loose.

113
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:37,560
As it fell to the ocean below, they were given just enough height to make it to the shores of Mysterious Island.

114
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:46,620
This story that I just shared with you illustrates the importance of what we think may be essential.

115
00:06:46,620 --> 00:06:49,740
What we think is a priority in life.

116
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:54,980
It literally may be something that is holding us back to getting to where God wants us to be.

117
00:06:54,980 --> 00:06:57,420
Did you ever think about it that way?

118
00:06:58,100 --> 00:07:05,580
And we want to then get into that book that we all had devotions in this morning, that Old Testament book of Haggai, right?

119
00:07:05,580 --> 00:07:09,000
Is that where you had your devotions this morning, the book of Haggai?

120
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:15,280
Well, if you don't know where it is, if you got a digital version, open it up, please, because I want you to have that text in front of you.

121
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:21,180
If you have a paper version that's that amazing thing called the table of contents, it always gets you to the right page.

122
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:25,920
So I want you to get that Bible open to the book of Haggai, chapter one.

123
00:07:25,920 --> 00:07:27,500
We're going to be right there in chapter one.

124
00:07:28,100 --> 00:07:36,340
And I want you to follow along with us, because the first half of the message, we're going to be focusing in on that chapter and looking at that.

125
00:07:36,340 --> 00:07:41,260
If you remember nothing more from this time together, I want you to remember this.

126
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:48,560
Because God cares about our priorities, our personal financial stewardship should reflect God's priorities.

127
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:50,300
That's how it should be.

128
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:56,260
And I want us to think about that in light of what we're going to be looking at in the book of Haggai, chapter one.

129
00:07:56,580 --> 00:08:02,080
So as we start off, follow along as I read to you, Haggai chapter one.

130
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:05,100
And I want to look at verses one through six first here.

131
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:10,060
And I want us to see misplaced priorities exposed.

132
00:08:10,060 --> 00:08:11,660
Follow along.

133
00:08:11,660 --> 00:08:15,740
In the second year of Darius the king, in the sixth month, in the first day of the month,

134
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:20,840
the word of the Lord came by the hand of Haggai the prophet to Zerubbabel, son of Sheetal,

135
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:24,520
governor of Judah, and to Joshua, son of Jehoshadak, the high priest.

136
00:08:24,520 --> 00:08:26,600
Thus saith the Lord of hosts.

137
00:08:26,760 --> 00:08:30,940
These people say, the time has not yet come to rebuild the house of the Lord.

138
00:08:30,940 --> 00:08:34,480
Then the word of the Lord came by the hand of Haggai the prophet.

139
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:39,900
Is it a time for you yourselves to dwell in your paneled houses while this house lies in ruins?

140
00:08:39,900 --> 00:08:45,420
Now, therefore, thus saith the Lord of hosts, consider your ways.

141
00:08:45,420 --> 00:08:47,820
You have sown much and harvested little.

142
00:08:47,820 --> 00:08:49,740
You eat, but you never have enough.

143
00:08:49,740 --> 00:08:51,860
You drink, but you never have your fill.

144
00:08:51,860 --> 00:08:54,280
You clothe yourselves, but no one is warm.

145
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:59,320
And he who earns wages does so to put them into a bag with holes.

146
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:03,480
We see here that Israel was given a task.

147
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:06,300
They were given a task to rebuild the temple.

148
00:09:06,300 --> 00:09:14,440
In 539 BC, Cyrus the Great captured Babylon and allowed Israel to return to Jerusalem that following year.

149
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:22,500
As we read in Ezra chapter 1, Cyrus wrote an edict instructing Israel, rebuild the temple of God.

150
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:26,260
But what we see here is the nation started to lose focus.

151
00:09:26,260 --> 00:09:35,080
The resettled nation started out well with the completion of the temple floor, but it stopped there.

152
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:39,340
You know, the people of Israel are just like you and I today.

153
00:09:39,340 --> 00:09:43,160
We start working on this project right over here, and we get in the middle of it.

154
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:46,540
And we happen to look over our shoulder, and we see this project over here.

155
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:49,180
And we get over here, and we start working on this project.

156
00:09:49,180 --> 00:09:53,760
And as we're over here, we say, oh, wait about, I got to start working on this one.

157
00:09:53,760 --> 00:09:55,860
And we get working on this project here.

158
00:09:55,860 --> 00:09:57,760
I see some of you smiling out there.

159
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:59,700
You know what I'm talking about.

160
00:09:59,700 --> 00:10:03,140
How many projects do you have started, and how many do you have completed?

161
00:10:03,820 --> 00:10:06,460
So, well, the nation of Israel was just like us.

162
00:10:06,460 --> 00:10:08,580
We do the same thing today.

163
00:10:08,580 --> 00:10:13,260
We start a project, and we look for another one, or we find another one.

164
00:10:13,260 --> 00:10:14,220
It grabs our attention.

165
00:10:14,660 --> 00:10:30,300
And as you've guessed, the project that grabbed the attention, the excitement of the nation of Israel was the rebuilding of their own houses, as we see in verse 4 there in the text, thus leaving the temple floor to collect dust.

166
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:35,560
And their new rebuilding project, it wasn't just a simple, basic home.

167
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:41,900
According to the biblical text here we have, they were building paneled or sealed houses.

168
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:44,880
What does that mean?

169
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:46,560
I like to say it this way.

170
00:10:46,560 --> 00:10:50,240
Lowe's and Home Depot back then were doing phenomenally well.

171
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:51,940
They were doing great.

172
00:10:51,940 --> 00:10:53,800
So what was their excuse?

173
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:58,360
If we look at the text, we can see Israel's underlying thinking was this.

174
00:10:58,360 --> 00:11:01,560
Well, God, the timing just isn't right.

175
00:11:01,560 --> 00:11:02,880
Imagine saying that to God.

176
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:05,360
How can we say this?

177
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:06,220
Look at verse 6.

178
00:11:06,220 --> 00:11:11,440
We see Israel had crop failure, hunger, drought, sickness, disease, financial distress.

179
00:11:12,460 --> 00:11:16,560
Israel had excuses, and they were all very, very good excuses.

180
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:28,780
Yet with the excuses just flowing from the nation of Israel, it's important to note that they had the time, they had the money, they had the resources to take care of their own homes.

181
00:11:29,740 --> 00:11:32,620
So what's the reality of their situation?

182
00:11:32,620 --> 00:11:34,880
Their priorities were not God's priorities.

183
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:38,820
Clearly, they put themselves before God.

184
00:11:38,820 --> 00:11:47,280
Money is that great barometer to show what we love and value most.

185
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:49,440
Money is that great barometer.

186
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:55,580
How our money is spent reveals the ultimate priorities of our heart.

187
00:11:55,580 --> 00:12:05,080
So a good key takeaway here in these six verses, our activities and our use of money expose our true priorities.

188
00:12:05,940 --> 00:12:10,180
Now, let's continue on, and let's look at verses 7 through 11.

189
00:12:10,180 --> 00:12:15,600
And as we look at that, let's look at the cost of misplaced priorities.

190
00:12:15,600 --> 00:12:18,140
Follow along, starting at verse 7.

191
00:12:18,140 --> 00:12:19,060
Look at your text there.

192
00:12:19,060 --> 00:12:22,320
Thus sayeth the Lord of hosts, consider your ways.

193
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:29,100
Go up to the hills and bring wood and build the house, that I may take pleasure in it, and that I may be glorified, says the Lord.

194
00:12:29,100 --> 00:12:31,460
You look for much, and behold, it came to little.

195
00:12:31,460 --> 00:12:34,080
And when you brought it home, I blew it away.

196
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:43,280
Why, declares the Lord of hosts, because of my house that lies in ruins, while each of you busies himself with his own house.

197
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:48,620
Therefore, the heavens above you have withheld the dew, and the earth has withheld its produce.

198
00:12:48,620 --> 00:12:59,280
And I have called for a drought on the land and on the hills, on the grain, the new wine, the oil, on what the ground brings forth, on man and beast, and on all of their labors.

199
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:03,600
So what was the real cause of Israel's struggles?

200
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:07,580
God wanted to get their attention.

201
00:13:07,580 --> 00:13:11,000
So what was God's plan to get Israel's attention?

202
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:18,780
According to what we see here in the text, verse 11 says, God brought about scarcity, loss, drought, weak harvest, and frustration.

203
00:13:18,780 --> 00:13:26,280
Israel had very real problems, which were a direct result of their misplaced priorities.

204
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:29,560
They were complaining to God about all that was happening around them.

205
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:33,800
They were saying that they didn't have the time, the money, the resources to rebuild the temple.

206
00:13:34,180 --> 00:13:40,100
And God steps through time and space, through the prophet Haggai, and speaks to the people.

207
00:13:40,100 --> 00:13:41,620
And I'm paraphrasing here.

208
00:13:41,620 --> 00:13:44,360
God says through Haggai, I know your problems.

209
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:46,380
I see your problems.

210
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:48,240
I understand your problems.

211
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:50,640
And I'm causing those problems.

212
00:13:50,640 --> 00:13:56,560
It's me, God, doing all this.

213
00:13:57,960 --> 00:14:08,560
Does that experience in Haggai's day seem like an experience that happens to us on a regular basis where we save and save and save and save for that rainy day like today?

214
00:14:09,360 --> 00:14:14,340
But yet it rains every single Tuesday, and it wipes it all away.

215
00:14:14,340 --> 00:14:27,240
While it's important to note that while God caused those problems to get their attention back on him, not every financial struggle that we go through is a result of misplaced priorities.

216
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:28,500
Make sure you know that.

217
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:39,740
So in our text, we read twice this phrase, consider your ways, in verse 5 and in verse 7, with only one verse in between.

218
00:14:39,740 --> 00:14:42,440
You think God's trying to get our attention on something?

219
00:14:42,440 --> 00:14:43,740
Clearly he is.

220
00:14:43,740 --> 00:14:45,360
What's he trying to say?

221
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:46,420
Take time.

222
00:14:46,420 --> 00:14:47,320
Pause.

223
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:48,100
Reflect.

224
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:50,860
Respond to what I am doing.

225
00:14:50,860 --> 00:14:59,360
